request.prompt:
You are the planning half of a model validation. The rule-based plan has already run and produced
the candidate findings below. You may ask for at most 4 more tool call(s), one at a
time, and you should ask for none unless a call would tell a validator something the plan did not.

Typical follow-ups: re-profiling one feature that drifted, or recomputing metrics on a
sub-population where the model may behave differently.

Candidate findings so far:
- L2 (contamination, from check_leakage): 1.2556% of the rows of 'test' also appear in 'train', against a contamination threshold of 0.50%; the held-out split is not held out

Artifacts already in the store (121 of them), by prefix:
calibration (4), calibration_intercept (2), calibration_slope (2), challenger (4), condition_number (1), csi (11), deciles (4), guidance (7), leakage (7), metrics (16), profile (10), psi (12), rule (1), run (12), threshold (17), vif (11)

Tools you may call, with the JSON schema of each tool's arguments:
[
 {
  "tool": "run_model",
  "description": "Run the package's subject in a capped subprocess and store what it wrote: stdout, stderr, duration and every file of the spec 3.3 contract under run.<file>.",
  "schema": {
   "additionalProperties": false,
   "description": "Arguments of ``run_model``.\n\nAttributes:\n    synthetic: How many rows to ask the subject to generate, for an offline run. Exactly\n        one of this and ``data_dir`` is given.\n    data_dir: Where the subject's real data is, for a ``--data`` run.\n    seed: Passed to the subject as ``--seed``; ``None`` leaves the subject's own default,\n        which is the seed ``package.yaml`` documents.",
   "properties": {
    "synthetic": {
     "anyOf": [
      {
       "type": "integer"
      },
      {
       "type": "null"
      }
     ],
     "default": null,
     "title": "Synthetic"
    },
    "data_dir": {
     "anyOf": [
      {
       "type": "string"
      },
      {
       "type": "null"
      }
     ],
     "default": null,
     "title": "Data Dir"
    },
    "seed": {
     "anyOf": [
      {
       "type": "integer"
      },
      {
       "type": "null"
      }
     ],
     "default": null,
     "title": "Seed"
    }
   },
   "title": "Args",
   "type": "object"
  }
 },
 {
  "tool": "profile_data",
  "description": "Profile each declared split -- schema, missingness, descriptive statistics -- and compare every feature and the score with the training split by PSI and CSI.",
  "schema": {
   "additionalProperties": false,
   "description": "Arguments of ``profile_data``.\n\nAttributes:\n    splits: Which splits to profile; ``None`` means every split the package declares.\n    features: Which features to compare; ``None`` means every declared feature the\n        subject's own screen left in ``data_<split>.csv``.",
   "properties": {
    "splits": {
     "anyOf": [
      {
       "items": {
        "type": "string"
       },
       "type": "array"
      },
      {
       "type": "null"
      }
     ],
     "default": null,
     "title": "Splits"
    },
    "features": {
     "anyOf": [
      {
       "items": {
        "type": "string"
       },
       "type": "array"
      },
      {
       "type": "null"
      }
     ],
     "default": null,
     "title": "Features"
    }
   },
   "title": "Args",
   "type": "object"
  }
 },
 {
  "tool": "compute_metrics",
  "description": "Recompute AUC, Gini, KS, Brier, log loss, calibration and decile separation from the subject's predictions for each split -- and, for a hazard subject, monthly CPR -- then check every threshold package.yaml declares.",
  "schema": {
   "$defs": {
    "Subpopulation": {
     "additionalProperties": false,
     "description": "A slice of one split, for the follow-up metrics the bounded loop asks for.\n\nAttributes:\n    column: The column to slice on. It must be in ``data_<split>.csv``, which holds the\n        features the model actually used plus the identifier and the target.\n    rule: ``below_median``, ``above_median`` or ``equals:<value>``.",
     "properties": {
      "column": {
       "title": "Column",
       "type": "string"
      },
      "rule": {
       "title": "Rule",
       "type": "string"
      }
     },
     "required": [
      "column",
      "rule"
     ],
     "title": "Subpopulation",
     "type": "object"
    }
   },
   "additionalProperties": false,
   "description": "Arguments of ``compute_metrics``.\n\nAttributes:\n    splits: Which splits to compute; ``None`` means every split the package declares.\n    subpopulation: A slice of each split to compute the scalar metrics on as well, for\n        the bounded follow-up loop's \"how does it do on the low-limit half\" question.",
   "properties": {
    "splits": {
     "anyOf": [
      {
       "items": {
        "type": "string"
       },
       "type": "array"
      },
      {
       "type": "null"
      }
     ],
     "default": null,
     "title": "Splits"
    },
    "subpopulation": {
     "anyOf": [
      {
       "$ref": "#/$defs/Subpopulation"
      },
      {
       "type": "null"
      }
     ],
     "default": null
    }
   },
   "title": "Args",
   "type": "object"
  }
 },
 {
  "tool": "check_leakage",
  "description": "Screen for leakage: declared feature timings, each feature's own AUC against the outcome, the share of test rows that also appear in train, and target-adjacent feature names.",
  "schema": {
   "additionalProperties": false,
   "description": "Arguments of ``check_leakage``.\n\nAttributes:\n    train_split: The split the single-feature screen is run on and overlap is measured\n        against.\n    test_split: The split whose rows are looked for in the training split.",
   "properties": {
    "train_split": {
     "default": "train",
     "title": "Train Split",
     "type": "string"
    },
    "test_split": {
     "default": "test",
     "title": "Test Split",
     "type": "string"
    }
   },
   "title": "Args",
   "type": "object"
  }
 },
 {
  "tool": "check_stability",
  "description": "Split the fitting data by the package's regime column and compare the champion's AUC and each feature's coefficient across regimes; report the score's PSI over time.",
  "schema": {
   "additionalProperties": false,
   "description": "Arguments of ``check_stability``.\n\nAttributes:\n    regime_column: Which column defines the regimes; ``None`` takes ``regime.column`` from\n        ``package.yaml``.\n    split: Which split to compare within; the fitting split by default, because that is\n        where a coefficient's meaning is decided.",
   "properties": {
    "regime_column": {
     "anyOf": [
      {
       "type": "string"
      },
      {
       "type": "null"
      }
     ],
     "default": null,
     "title": "Regime Column"
    },
    "split": {
     "default": "train",
     "title": "Split",
     "type": "string"
    }
   },
   "title": "Args",
   "type": "object"
  }
 },
 {
  "tool": "check_collinearity",
  "description": "Compute each retained feature's variance inflation factor and Belsley's condition number of the column-standardised design matrix.",
  "schema": {
   "additionalProperties": false,
   "description": "Arguments of ``check_collinearity``.\n\nAttributes:\n    split: Which split's feature matrix to measure; the fitting split by default.\n    features: Which features to include; ``None`` means every declared feature the\n        subject's own screen left in the matrix.",
   "properties": {
    "split": {
     "default": "train",
     "title": "Split",
     "type": "string"
    },
    "features": {
     "anyOf": [
      {
       "items": {
        "type": "string"
       },
       "type": "array"
      },
      {
       "type": "null"
      }
     ],
     "default": null,
     "title": "Features"
    }
   },
   "title": "Args",
   "type": "object"
  }
 },
 {
  "tool": "challenger_compare",
  "description": "Fit a histogram gradient-boosting challenger on the same feature matrix the champion used and compare its test AUC and Brier score with the champion's.",
  "schema": {
   "additionalProperties": false,
   "description": "Arguments of ``challenger_compare``.\n\nAttributes:\n    train_split: Which split to fit the challenger on.\n    test_split: Which split to compare on.\n    seed: The challenger's random state.",
   "properties": {
    "train_split": {
     "default": "train",
     "title": "Train Split",
     "type": "string"
    },
    "test_split": {
     "default": "test",
     "title": "Test Split",
     "type": "string"
    },
    "seed": {
     "default": 20260901,
     "title": "Seed",
     "type": "integer"
    }
   },
   "title": "Args",
   "type": "object"
  }
 },
 {
  "tool": "run_scenarios",
  "description": "Read the hazard subject's projection, recompute the servicing value change at each declared rate shock and the convexity of the curve, and check both against the convexity the package declares.",
  "schema": {
   "additionalProperties": false,
   "description": "Arguments of ``run_scenarios``.\n\nAttributes:\n    expectation: Which way the value curve is expected to bend, overriding\n        ``scenarios.convexity_expectation``; ``None`` uses the package's own declaration,\n        which is the only thing a validation should normally test against.",
   "properties": {
    "expectation": {
     "anyOf": [
      {
       "type": "string"
      },
      {
       "type": "null"
      }
     ],
     "default": null,
     "title": "Expectation"
    }
   },
   "title": "Args",
   "type": "object"
  }
 },
 {
  "tool": "retrieve_guidance",
  "description": "Search the committed regulatory corpus (SR 11-7 and its 2026 revision SR 26-2) with BM25 and return the best-matching sections, so a report section can be anchored to the guidance with a [[reg:DOC:SECTION]] citation.",
  "schema": {
   "additionalProperties": false,
   "description": "Arguments of ``retrieve_guidance``.\n\nAttributes:\n    query: What to look for, in plain words -- ``\"outcomes analysis\"``,\n        ``\"benchmarking against a challenger model\"``.\n    k: How many spans to return, at most.\n    docs: Restrict the search to these documents; ``None`` searches both. ``SR26-2`` is\n        the current guidance and ``SR11-7`` the superseded text kept so that historical\n        citations resolve (DECISIONS D-055).",
   "properties": {
    "query": {
     "title": "Query",
     "type": "string"
    },
    "k": {
     "default": 3,
     "title": "K",
     "type": "integer"
    },
    "docs": {
     "anyOf": [
      {
       "items": {
        "type": "string"
       },
       "type": "array"
      },
      {
       "type": "null"
      }
     ],
     "default": null,
     "title": "Docs"
    }
   },
   "required": [
    "query"
   ],
   "title": "Args",
   "type": "object"
  }
 }
]

Answer with either {"tool": "<name>", "args": {...}, "why": "<one clause>"} or {"stop": true}.
An action naming a tool that is not listed, arguments the schema does not allow, or a path outside
the package will be refused and recorded as refused.

Answer with one JSON object and nothing else: no prose before or after it, no explanation, no markdown fence. It must validate against this JSON schema:
{"additionalProperties": false, "description": "One action of the bounded loop, exactly as spec section 3.12 writes it.\n\nAttributes:\n    tool: The tool to call, or ``None`` when stopping.\n    args: Its arguments.\n    why: Why this call is worth making.\n    stop: ``True`` to end the loop.", "properties": {"tool": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "title": "Tool"}, "args": {"additionalProperties": true, "title": "Args", "type": "object"}, "why": {"default": "", "title": "Why", "type": "string"}, "stop": {"default": false, "title": "Stop", "type": "boolean"}}, "title": "FollowUpAction", "type": "object"}
